{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>I see him but not now.</b> He prophesied concerning David." "<b>I behold him but not near.</b> It is a doubling of the word." "<b>The course of a star from Jacob.</b> An expression of going, like הארץ אשר דרך בה. It already explained that the stars held to their course to come to help Israel." "<b>And a scepter.</b> The <b>scepter</b> and the dominion have already risen from Israel." "<b>And smite the corners of Moab.</b> etc. An analogy: the stars fought Sisera from their courses. <b>And smite the corners of Moab</b> — he continues prophesying that in the future Israel will yet inherit Edom, Moab, and Ammon, just as HaShem stipulated to Avram in the covenant between the pieces: את הקיני את הקניזי ואת הקדמוני — these are Ammon, Moab, and Edom." "<b>And he shall crush all the children of Shet.</b> One may say: these are the children of Moab, for they are children of nakedness and harlotry, from the root meaning חשופי שת (those whose private parts are exposed)."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:37.904591235Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}